  "id": "insulin",
  "term": "insulin",
  "definition": "Insulin is a peripheral hormone signal that the hypothalamic arcuate nucleus helps integrate with other body and neural signals to regulate food intake and energy use. When this signaling is dysregulated, it may contribute to persistently increased appetite and reduced energy expenditure.",
